    summary: 'The TLB caches recent virtual-to-physical translations so most accesses skip the page-table walk. Its capacity is small (on the order of a few thousand entries), so with 4 KB pages it covers only a few MB; huge pages (2 MB, or 1 GB) multiply the reach. A page fault is the kernel path taken when a translation is missing or disallowed: minor faults allocate or map an existing page in microseconds, major faults wait on disk.',
